$$ Having introduced the oriented distance, we can replace eq.(6.4) with the following one: $$
\forall \mathbf {p} \in \mathcal {M} _ {N}; \quad \mathfrak {p} (Y = 1 \mid \mathbf {X} = \mathbf {p}, \boldsymbol {\theta}) = \mathfrak {p} (\mathbf {p}; \boldsymbol {\theta}) = \sigma (\widehat {\delta} (\mathbf {p}, \mathfrak {S} [ \boldsymbol {\theta} ])) \tag {6.16}
